# Cloudflare Pages/Workers redirect rules. These are evaluated BEFORE static
# assets. Status 301 rules upgrade the Astro-generated meta-refresh pages
# (which remain in the build as a fallback for non-Cloudflare hosting) to real
# 301s that preserve search-engine link equity. Status 200 rules are rewrites:
# Cloudflare serves the target page's HTML at the requested URL without
# redirecting.
#
# Rules must match the request path exactly, so each old URL is listed both
# with and without its trailing slash.

# Site root is handled by functions/_middleware.ts (Accept-Language based
# redirect to the best published locale's introduction page), which runs before
# these rules and never falls through to them for "/" — no rule needed here.
#
# Locale roots: one 301 for the slashless form plus one 200 rewrite that serves
# the locale's introduction page at its own root. Rules are static, so each new
# locale listed with `docsTree: true` in src/constants/docsLocales.ts needs its
# own pair here; the Astro redirect map is generated from that table and this
# file is not. See docs/en/contributing/adding-locale/documentation.md.
#
# Every target locale is listed here ahead of its page tree, so a translation
# lane never edits this file. Until that locale's `docsTree` flag flips, the
# rewrite target does not exist and the root serves a 404, which is the honest
# answer for a URL with no content behind it.

# Japanese locale root
/ja /ja/ 301
/ja/ /ja/introduction/ 200

# Target locale roots, staged for the language-expansion translation lanes
/pt-BR /pt-BR/ 301
/pt-BR/ /pt-BR/introduction/ 200
/es-419 /es-419/ 301
/es-419/ /es-419/introduction/ 200
/fr /fr/ 301
/fr/ /fr/introduction/ 200
/zh-TW /zh-TW/ 301
/zh-TW/ /zh-TW/introduction/ 200
/zh-CN /zh-CN/ 301
/zh-CN/ /zh-CN/introduction/ 200
/vi /vi/ 301
/vi/ /vi/introduction/ 200
/ru /ru/ 301
/ru/ /ru/introduction/ 200
/ko /ko/ 301
/ko/ /ko/introduction/ 200

